module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.lens_prices_the_authority_while_the_lane_runs_the_realization

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data lens_prices_the_authority_while_the_lane_runs_the_realization: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "lens_prices_the_authority_while_the_lane_runs_the_realization" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "A COST LENS READS THE AUTHORITY AND THE LANE RUNS THE REALIZATION, so a verdict about one is cited as a fact about the other. The invalid state is a lens verdict presented as a cost fact when the declaration it priced and the code that executes have different cost shapes. The harm is worse than a wrong number, because the verdict is directional: it can convict a construction that is fast and acquit one that is quadratic, and it is cited as coverage in both cases. ",
    "MEASURED BOTH DIRECTIONS ON ONE SUBJECT, v2.compiler.tokenize, 2026-09-10, required-v2-native lane. FALSE NEGATIVE, pre-repair: the accumulator-copy lens over the file carrying the quadratic per-chunk lexeme accumulation reported suspect_sites 0 and refusal_sites 1 (combiner_unregistered_carrier_reaches) -- it did not see the accumulator because the accumulator was a RECORD FIELD (RepeatState.lexeme) rather than a bare parameter, and it refused rather than convicting. Fail-closed, and not detection. FALSE POSITIVE, post-repair: the same lens over the repaired file reported suspect_sites 1, convicting lexeme_grow's per-character list_snoc_item -- the construction measured linear on the executing binary. ",
    "THE MECHANISM IS A DIVERGENCE BETWEEN THREE CARRIERS OF ONE COST FACT, and each was read rather than assumed. std.algebra list_snoc_item is `xs |> list_push(item)` since the FreeMonoid primitive routing; std.primitives list_push_contract declares persistent_work `log n`; the emitted realization is v1_rt::rc_list_push, an Rc::make_mut push_back on a persistent vector. Those three agree. std.primitives concat_contract, by contrast, declares work `n + m` while the realization charges the RIGHT operand only -- so the model prices an accumulate-on-the-left concat fold as quadratic where the executing code is linear in the appended side. A lens consuming that contract convicts the correct construction. ",
    "WHY IT IS NOT AN ORDINARY STALE-COMMENT DEFECT: nothing here is prose. Every carrier is a modeled declaration, each internally consistent, and the divergence is only visible by joining a contract to its realization to a measurement. std.nat states that rc_list_concat clones every element of its right operand; gunbc.build_target states that make_mut shares structure rather than copying the spine -- both are partly right, because make_mut's clone of the LEFT is structural sharing while the extend of the RIGHT is per-element. The executing bridge is src/v1/stage0/src/v1_rt.rs rc_list_concat: make_mut the left, extend by cloning the right. v2.std.fn_index callee_texts_in_subtree used to concatenate child-then-accumulator on a left-charging reading; after list_append routed to concat that cloned the growing acc, and the walk now combines acc-then-child so first-occurrence order matches node_subtree_nodes and the copied side is the child. The remaining fork is concat_contract (n+m) versus that realization. build_target's own text closes by saying it is a reading of two carriers and not a measurement, which is the honest label. ",
    "THE REVIEW TELL, and it is cheap: a cost verdict cited without naming which carrier produced it. A lens verdict is a claim about a DECLARATION under a COST MODEL; a timing is a claim about a REALIZATION on a MACHINE. Neither is evidence for the other, and a report that says only 'this is quadratic' has dropped the field that decides whether it can be believed. The same rule the design document already applies to measurements -- name the instrument -- applies to cost classes: name the contract. The realization timing for list_append concat vs reconstructed fold_list_right is re-derived by gunbc.instruments.list_append_concat_paired_timing paired_timing (gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/gunbc/instruments/list_append_concat_paired_timing.dag --function paired_timing), not transcribed here. ",
    "THE CONSEQUENCE FOR ENROLMENT, which is what this row exists to block. A corpus gate over src/v2/compiler built on a cost model that convicts the repaired construction and acquits the broken one is not a weak wall, it is an active hazard: it would fail the lane on correct code and pass it on the defect it was built for. The next-rung trigger is therefore not the gate but the model -- the cost model must price list_push by its primitive routing AND see a record-field accumulator carrier -- and until both hold, a suspect count from this lens is not evidence of absence and a refusal cause is not evidence of anything. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
